{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Science or Science Fiction?", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Movie Magic", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "If \u2026 Are to /Were to ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">if + am/is/are/were to \u2026</span> to suggest that you have very little influence over the outcome of a situation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Supposing you are to make a movie, how will you spend the money?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">If + am/is/are to \u2026 </span> is used to suggest that the condition may or may not be fulfilled.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">If you are to have special effects, what type will they be?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">If + were to \u2026</span> is used to suggest that the condition is very unlikely to be fulfilled.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">If you were to come up with some of the more famous special effects, what movies would they be from?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can replace <span class=\"italic\">if</span> with <span class=\"italic\">were</span>. This is not possible with <span class=\"italic\">am/is/are</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Were you to come up with some of the more famous special effects, what movies would they be from?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Were I to cite films whose effects have filled us with wonder, I would start with Avatar and The Life of Pi. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Were it not for the magic, these films would not have been the same.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Prepositions + -ing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you talk about two actions linked together, you normally use two verbs. When you use prepositional verbs, the second verb is always in the -ing form.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Since then moviemakers have succeeded in producing even more amazing effects, depending on having enough time and money, of course. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You can use two verbs to talk about two connected actions. The main verb introduces the main action, and the second verb in the -ing form gives more information about that action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepositional verbs are always followed by another verb in the -ing form like <span class=\"italic\">end up, carry on, keep on, go on, succeed in, depend on, adjust to, put off \u2026</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structure: <br> Subject + prepositional verb + -ing form of the second verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at some examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Stars now adjust to acting with green screens.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "With Avatar, James Cameron put off starting the film until new techniques had advanced far enough to portray his vision.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to construct ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to build", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In early films like <span class=\"italic\">The Ten Commandments</span> special effects artists spent money on constructing a U-shaped water tank to film the parting of the sea.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk special effects in films", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "bells and whistles", "type": "name"}, {"content": "special features added to attract customers", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"italic\">Casablanca</span> just doesn't have the bells and whistles.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "superhero ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "characters in stories or movies who have special powers, help people, and fight evil", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are now used to having our superheros really fly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "profusely ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "with a large amount of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Tom complained profusely about watching the movie.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "mediocre ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "acceptable, but not enough", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This movie is mediocre at best. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "jaded ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " \u200blacking \u200binterest or \u200bdesire because of having experienced so much ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We were jaded after watching the horror movie.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "ultra-heightened ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "highly increased", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have a ultra-heightened sense of paranoia after watching the movie. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "suspension ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act of stopping or freezing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You needed a suspension of disbelief when watching the movie.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Go online or to the library and find out how early films produced special effects.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the year they were produced.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out how the films were received and whether people were excited about the special effects then. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare a short talk on how special effects and the way they are received have changed.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your ideas with a group or a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I find out how early films produced special effects.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I find out how the films were received and whether people were excited about the special effects then. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I prepare a short talk on special effects.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my ideas with a partner or group", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn11le04ob10re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn11le04ob10re2img01.jpg", "time": "", "id": 1, "text": "Supposing you are to make a movie, how will you spend the money? If you are to have special effects, what type will they be? Creating special effects is becoming more and more common in the movie industry. Were you to come up with some of the more famous special effects, what movies would they be from? In early films like <span class=\"italic\">The Ten Commandments</span> special effects artists spent money on constructing a  U-shaped water tank to film the parting of the sea. Since then moviemakers have succeeded in producing even more amazing effects, depending on having enough time and money, of course."}, {"image": "engenn11le04ob10re2img02.jpg", "time": "42000", "id": 2, "text": "Stars now adjust to acting with green screens. Were I to cite films whose effects have filled us with wonder, I would start with <span class=\"italic\">Avatar</span> and <span class=\"italic\">The Life of Pi</span>. Were it not for the magic, these films would not have been the same. With<span class=\"italic\"> Avatar</span>, James Cameron put off starting the film until new techniques had advanced far enough to portray his vision. In <span class=\"italic\">The Life of Pi </span>they succeeded in combining green screens and animation. This succeeded in opening a new chapter in filmmaking. The sky, it seems, is now the limit. Were I to open up the list to other FX epics, I am sure they would offer up <span class=\"italic\">Jurassic</span> anything, <span class=\"italic\">Independence Day</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Alien</span> and its siblings, <span class=\"italic\">Transformers</span> and any superhero saga."}, {"image": "engenn11le04ob10re2img03.jpg", "time": "95000", "id": 3, "text": "We are now used to having our superheros really fly. We believe in demanding the best, most up-to-date effects. We complain profusely about watching anything slightly mediocre. Supposing you subject a group of teens to a series of classic black and white films, what would their reaction be? Disbelief, anger, boredom? We are jaded by the ultra-heightened suspension of reality. <span class=\"italic\">Casablanca</span> just doesn't have the bells and whistles."}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le04ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le04ob10re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about art, science, exploration, beliefs and opinions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express that I have no influence over whether a condition will be fulfilled.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about two actions together.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What film has had the best special effects so far in your opinion?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What new effects would you like to see in films in the future?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Special effects in films are fascinating!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " How many FX films can you <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">cite</span>?", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content"